== args
NiceMon V9.9
? lists the commands
> tftp
tftp IP NAME: the server and the file, such as tftp 192.168.1.10 hello.bin
> tftp x
tftp IP NAME: the server and the file, such as tftp 192.168.1.10 hello.bin
> tftp 10.0.0.2
tftp IP NAME: the server and the file, such as tftp 192.168.1.10 hello.bin
> tftp 10.0.0.2 a b
tftp IP NAME: the server and the file, such as tftp 192.168.1.10 hello.bin
> tftp 10.0.0.256 a
tftp IP NAME: the server and the file, such as tftp 192.168.1.10 hello.bin
> tftp 10.0.0.2x a
tftp IP NAME: the server and the file, such as tftp 192.168.1.10 hello.bin
